emulator are downloaded from Google by `tools/bootstrap_android.ps1` and are
governed by Google's terms; they are not redistributed here.

Data tables
-----------

`server/app/protocol/roguelike_events.py` and
`server/app/protocol/roguelike_exports.py` contain small factual mappings
(numeric event and reward identifiers) recovered from the client's own data
files. They are included because a server cannot interoperate without them.
They are regenerated from a locally supplied copy by the scripts in `tools/`,
and the tests that verify them are gated behind the `preservation_artifact`
marker precisely so that a clean checkout never requires the original.

Decryption and patching tools
-----------------------------

`tools/cocos_jsc.py` decrypts the client's script bundle with a key the
operator supplies. `tools/cn_client_patch.py` patches the operator's own local
copy so that it logs in to the local server instead of the publisher's retired
login service. They are provided only for personal, offline use of a
lawfully obtained copy of a game whose official servers have shut down.
Whether that use is lawful depends on the operator's jurisdiction; operators
are responsible for checking their local law and for how they use the tools.

